Service is running on port 8080.
Find which Tomcat instance is running it.

1. Find the Java process listening on port 8080
ss -tulpn | grep 8080
Output:
tcp LISTEN ... users:(("java",pid=12345,...))

2. Get the Java process details
ps -fp 12345
or
ps -ef | grep 12345

3. Identify the Tomcat instance
Look for one of the following JVM options:
-Dcatalina.home=
-Dcatalina.base=

Example:
java \
 -Dcatalina.home=/opt/tomcat9 \
 -Dcatalina.base=/opt/tomcat_instances/app1

This tells you which Tomcat installation/instance is running.
